## HLD vs. LLD
5:39 System design has two levels: High-Level Design (HLD) and Low-Level Design (LLD). 5:44 High-Level Design is the zoomed-out view, the architecture, the big boxes. 5:56 It's about app servers, databases, caches, queues, and how they talk to each other. 6:01 Low-Level Design is the zoomed-in view, the code, the class structures, the data objects. 6:44 These are two different skills, but both are essential.

